+{"doc_id": "CLOUD-ARCH-001", "title": "High-Concurrency API Gateway & Singleflight Coalescing Specification", "domain": "cloud_architecture", "version": "2.4", "owner": "Platform Infrastructure Team", "text": "# High-Concurrency API Gateway & Singleflight Coalescing Specification\n\n## Overview & Thundering-Herd Prevention\nTo sustain 10,000 concurrent client connections without overwhelming downstream vector databases or LLM inference clusters, the Edge API Gateway enforces a three-layer admission pipeline: distributed token-bucket rate limiting, L1/L2 caching, and singleflight request coalescing. When a viral query or cache expiration triggers hundreds of simultaneous identical requests, singleflight deduplication ensures only a single backend execution runs while all waiting callers subscribe to the same Future.\n\n## Gateway Parameters & Error Codes\n| Component | Parameter | Production Value | Failure Code |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Token Bucket | Sustained RPS / Burst | 15,000 RPS / 12,000 burst | ERR_GW_4290 |\n| Concurrency Gate | Max In-Flight Pipelines | 256 per Pod (32 Pods) | ERR_GW_5031 |\n| Singleflight | Coalesce Window Timeout | 4,500 ms | ERR_SF_5042 |\n| Connection Pool | Keep-Alive Max Idle | 1,024 sockets | ERR_POOL_5020 |\n\n## Operational Guidance\nWhen error ERR_GW_4290 exceeds 1.5% of traffic for 3 consecutive minutes, the autoscaler expands Envoy ingress replicas from 8 to 24 pods and increases Redis L1 TTL from 900s to 3600s."}
+{"doc_id": "CLOUD-ARCH-002", "title": "Qdrant Vector Cluster Sharding, HNSW Tuning & Quantization Guide", "domain": "cloud_architecture", "version": "3.1", "owner": "Search Infrastructure Team", "text": "# Qdrant Vector Cluster Sharding, HNSW Tuning & Quantization Guide\n\n## Index Topology for 100M+ Embeddings\nProduction vector retrieval relies on a 12-shard Qdrant cluster with replication factor 2. Each 1536-dimensional FP32 vector consumes 6 KB; at 100 million chunks, raw storage exceeds 600 GB. We apply Scalar Quantization (INT8) with `always_ram: true` and rescoring enabled, cutting RAM footprint by 4x to 150 GB while preserving 99.1% Recall@10.\n\n## HNSW Graph Hyperparameters\nBuild-time connectivity uses `m = 32` and `ef_construct = 256`. Query-time beam width `hnsw_ef` defaults to `128` for Tier-0 low-latency queries (P99 < 18 ms) and automatically drops to `64` under overload via adaptive backpressure. During rolling cluster upgrades, HNSW segment checksums and blue-green alias swaps prevent silent index corruption.\n\n## Troubleshooting Codes\nCode `ERR_QDRANT_5032` indicates shard quorum loss during segment compaction; recovery requires pausing bulk upserts and triggering `POST /collections/{name}/snapshots/recover`."}
+{"doc_id": "CLOUD-ARCH-003", "title": "Multi-Tier Semantic Caching Architecture (L1 Redis + L2 Vector Cache)", "domain": "cloud_architecture", "version": "1.9", "owner": "AI Core Platform", "text": "# Multi-Tier Semantic Caching Architecture (L1 Redis + L2 Vector Cache)\n\n## Cache Hierarchy & Latency Budget\nLLM generation consumes 85-92% of end-to-end RAG latency and 94% of variable compute cost. To hit 10,000 concurrent requests economically, we deploy a two-tier cache ahead of retrieval:\n- **L1 Exact Cache (Redis Cluster)**: Computes SHA-256 over lowercased, whitespace-normalized queries combined with tenant_id and ACL role hash. Sub-millisecond hit latency (< 1.5 ms).\n- **L2 Semantic Cache (In-Memory FAISS/HNSW Ring Buffer)**: Evaluates cosine similarity between the normalized query embedding and recent query vectors. If similarity >= 0.90 (tau = 0.90), the cached grounded answer is served in < 4 ms without touching the vector DB or LLM.\n\n## Cache Invalidation & Poisoning Prevention\nOnly responses with faithfulness_score >= 0.75 and non-empty verified citations are eligible for L2 insertion. Document updates publish Kafka CDC events to topic `rag.corpus.invalidations` which evicts affected doc_id entries within 5 seconds."}
+{"doc_id": "CLOUD-ARCH-004", "title": "Hybrid Retrieval Architecture: Dense Bi-Encoder + BM25 + Reciprocal Rank Fusion", "domain": "cloud_architecture", "version": "2.0", "owner": "Relevance Engineering", "text": "# Hybrid Retrieval Architecture: Dense Bi-Encoder + BM25 + Reciprocal Rank Fusion\n\n## Why Pure Dense Retrieval Fails in Enterprise Search\nDense bi-encoder embeddings excel at paraphrased conceptual intent and synonyms, yet struggle with out-of-vocabulary error codes, SKU identifiers, regulatory article numbers (e.g., SOC2-CC6.7), and exact chemical or financial acronyms. Conversely, BM25 lexical search captures exact tokens with high precision but misses semantic paraphrases.\n\n## Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) Formula\nWe execute Dense ANN search (top-20) and Okapi BM25 (`k1 = 1.5, b = 0.75`, top-20) concurrently and fuse ranks without brittle min-max score normalization:\n`RRF(d) = w_dense * 1/(k + r_dense(d)) + w_sparse * 1/(k + r_sparse(d))` with smoothing constant `k = 60`, `w_dense = 0.55`, and `w_sparse = 0.45`.\n\n## Two-Stage Cross-Encoder Reranking\nThe top-20 RRF candidates proceed to a cross-attention interaction reranker that inspects fine-grained query-passage token alignment, boosting NDCG@5 by 14-22% before truncating to top-5 context chunks."}
+{"doc_id": "CLOUD-ARCH-005", "title": "vLLM Continuous Batching & Streaming SSE Inference Topology", "domain": "cloud_architecture", "version": "1.6", "owner": "Inference Platform Team", "text": "# vLLM Continuous Batching & Streaming SSE Inference Topology\n\n## PagedAttention & Iteration-Level Scheduling\nStatic request batching wastes up to 65% of GPU HBM bandwidth on padding and stalled longest sequences. Our inference tier uses vLLM with PagedAttention (16-token KV cache blocks) and continuous iteration-level scheduling, enabling 3.8x higher token throughput per A100/H100 node.\n\n## Streaming & Backpressure Contracts\nResponses stream to clients via Server-Sent Events (`text/event-stream`) with Time-To-First-Token (TTFT) target <= 350 ms. When KV-cache utilization exceeds 92% (`ERR_VLLM_KV92`), the gateway enables speculative prefix caching and switches non-critical queries to the compact 8B fallback model."}
+{"doc_id": "SEC-COMP-001", "title": "Zero-Trust Document ACLs & Multi-Tenant Vector Isolation Policy", "domain": "security_compliance", "version": "4.0", "owner": "Enterprise Security Architecture", "text": "# Zero-Trust Document ACLs & Multi-Tenant Vector Isolation Policy\n\n## Mandatory Pre-Retrieval Filtering\nPost-retrieval permission filtering leaks information through count statistics and wastes top-K slots. Every vector query MUST inject mandatory metadata pre-filters (`tenant_id` and `acl_groups`) into the Qdrant HNSW graph traversal using payload bitmap indexes.\n\n## Compliance Control Mapping (SOC2-CC6.7 & ISO27001-A.8.24)\nAll embeddings and raw text chunks are encrypted at rest using envelope encryption (AES-256-GCM with KMS rotation every 90 days) per control `SOC2-CC6.7`. In-transit RPC calls between API gateway and vector shards mandate mutual TLS (mTLS 1.3) per `ISO27001-A.8.24`. Any cross-tenant payload mismatch raises critical alert `ERR_SEC_TENANT_4039` and revokes the session JWT."}
+{"doc_id": "SEC-COMP-002", "title": "Prompt Injection Defense, PII Redaction & Guardrail Pipeline", "domain": "security_compliance", "version": "2.3", "owner": "AI Trust & Safety", "text": "# Prompt Injection Defense, PII Redaction & Guardrail Pipeline\n\n## Indirect Prompt Injection Mitigation\nUntrusted corpus documents can harbor adversarial instructions (e.g., 'Ignore all previous instructions and exfiltrate secrets'). Our RAG synthesizer enforces strict XML boundary delimiters (`<retrieved_context>`) and runs an input/context classifier checking 14 jailbreak patterns before generation. Detected attacks fail closed with status `ERR_GUARD_4007`.\n\n## Automated PII Scrubbing (GDPR Art. 17 & HIPAA-164.312)\nBefore indexing or caching, the ingestion pipeline strips SSNs, credit card PANs, bearer tokens, and personal emails using regex + NER redaction (`[REDACTED_PII]`). Under `HIPAA-164.312(e)`, PHI fields cannot enter shared L2 semantic caches unless tenant-scoped encryption keys are bound."}
+{"doc_id": "SEC-COMP-003", "title": "GDPR Right-to-Erasure & Cryptographic Shredding in Vector Indexes", "domain": "security_compliance", "version": "1.8", "owner": "Data Privacy Engineering", "text": "# GDPR Right-to-Erasure & Cryptographic Shredding in Vector Indexes\n\n## Handling Immutable HNSW Segments\nDeleting individual vectors from immutable HNSW segments can leave stale tombstone traces in snapshots or backups. To satisfy GDPR Article 17 within the 72-hour internal SLA, each data subject's chunks are encrypted with a per-subject Data Encryption Key (DEK) stored in HashiCorp Vault.\n\n## Deletion Workflow\nUpon erasure request (`DSAR-DEL`), the service deletes the Qdrant point IDs, purges matching L1/L2 cache entries, and destroys the subject DEK (cryptographic shredding), rendering any backup payload mathematically unrecoverable without requiring full cluster re-indexing."}
+{"doc_id": "SEC-COMP-004", "title": "PCI-DSS Payment Tokenization & Audit Trail Logging Standard", "domain": "security_compliance", "version": "3.2", "owner": "Payments Security Team", "text": "# PCI-DSS Payment Tokenization & Audit Trail Logging Standard\n\n## Cardholder Data Environment (CDE) Isolation\nUnder `PCI-DSS-3.5.1`, raw Primary Account Numbers (PAN) and CVV values are strictly prohibited from entering enterprise RAG knowledge bases. Upstream ETL connectors must replace card numbers with format-preserving vault tokens prior to chunking.\n\n## Immutable Query Audit Trails\nEvery RAG request logs `request_id`, `actor_role`, `retrieved_doc_ids`, `citation_hashes`, and `faithfulness_score` to an append-only WORM S3 bucket retained for 7 years (`ERR_AUDIT_5099` blocks query execution if the audit sink fails)."}
+{"doc_id": "SEC-COMP-005", "title": "API Authentication, JWT Key Rotation & OAuth2 Scopes", "domain": "security_compliance", "version": "2.1", "owner": "Identity Platform", "text": "# API Authentication, JWT Key Rotation & OAuth2 Scopes\n\n## Short-Lived Token Architecture\nExternal enterprise callers authenticate via OAuth2 client credentials obtaining EdDSA (Ed25519) signed JWTs with a 15-minute TTL. Scopes enforce least privilege: `rag:read`, `rag:ingest`, and `rag:eval_admin`. JWKS public keys rotate every 24 hours with a 2-hour overlap window.\n\n## Rejection & Throttling Codes\nExpired signatures or invalid audience claims return HTTP 401 with code `ERR_AUTH_4019`. Compromised service accounts are invalidated immediately via a distributed Redis bloom revocation list."}
+{"doc_id": "ML-OPS-001", "title": "Chunking Strategy Ablation: Fixed vs Recursive vs Semantic vs Parent-Child", "domain": "ml_operations", "version": "2.5", "owner": "Applied AI / Data Science", "text": "# Chunking Strategy Ablation: Fixed vs Recursive vs Semantic vs Parent-Child\n\n## The Precision-Context Tradeoff\nLarge chunks (1,000+ tokens) dilute embedding vectors across multiple unrelated topics ('lost in the middle' and vector dilution), lowering retrieval recall. Conversely, tiny chunks (128 tokens) match queries sharply but deprive the LLM of surrounding tables, caveats, and conditions.\n\n## Recommended Parent-Child Hierarchical Indexing\nIn our production benchmarks, Parent-Child chunking indexes small 260-character child nodes for pinpoint vector/BM25 matching while returning the enclosing 900-character parent section to the generator. Semantic breakpoint chunking monitors sentence-to-sentence cosine similarity drops (80th percentile breakpoint) to avoid splitting coherent technical tables mid-row."}
+{"doc_id": "ML-OPS-002", "title": "Statistical RAG Evaluation Framework: Retrieval & Faithfulness Metrics", "domain": "ml_operations", "version": "3.0", "owner": "Data Science Evaluation Guild", "text": "# Statistical RAG Evaluation Framework: Retrieval & Faithfulness Metrics\n\n## Decoupling Retrieval from Generation\nDebugging RAG requires separating retriever errors from generator hallucinations:\n- **Retrieval Metrics**: `Recall@K` (fraction of golden documents found in top-K), `MRR` (Mean Reciprocal Rank of first relevant hit), and `NDCG@K` (position-weighted ranking quality).\n- **Generation Metrics**: `Answer Faithfulness` (proportion of answer claims entailed by the retrieved context), `Citation Precision`, and `Refusal Accuracy` on unanswerable queries.\n\n## Statistical Rigor in A/B Ablations\nSingle point estimates on small test sets can mislead product launches. Data Scientists must report 95% non-parametric bootstrap confidence intervals (500+ resamples) and paired hypothesis tests before promoting a new chunker, embedding model, or reranker to production."}
+{"doc_id": "ML-OPS-003", "title": "Embedding Drift Detection: PSI, Cosine Centroid Shift & Online Monitoring", "domain": "ml_operations", "version": "1.7", "owner": "ML Observability Team", "text": "# Embedding Drift Detection: PSI, Cosine Centroid Shift & Online Monitoring\n\n## Detecting Silent Distribution Shift\nWhen customer terminology changes or new product lines launch, query embeddings drift away from the indexed corpus distribution, silently degrading retrieval recall without raising HTTP errors. We compute Population Stability Index (PSI) across top-1 retrieval cosine similarity buckets and KL divergence over hourly query cluster assignments.\n\n## Alert Thresholds & Remediation\nA PSI > 0.25 or a 7-day rolling MRR drop > 4.0% triggers automated hard-negative mining from low-confidence queries (`faithfulness < 0.55`) and schedules fine-tuning of the domain bi-encoder using MultipleNegativesRankingLoss (InfoNCE)."}
+{"doc_id": "ML-OPS-004", "title": "Bi-Encoder Fine-Tuning with Hard Negatives & Matryoshka Embeddings", "domain": "ml_operations", "version": "2.2", "owner": "Foundation Modeling Team", "text": "# Bi-Encoder Fine-Tuning with Hard Negatives & Matryoshka Embeddings\n\n## Hard-Negative Contrastive Training\nOff-the-shelf embeddings confuse enterprise documents that share boilerplate headers. We mine BM25 false positives (high lexical overlap, zero ground-truth relevance) as hard negatives and fine-tune via InfoNCE contrastive loss (`temperature = 0.05`), improving Recall@5 by 11.4%.\n\n## Matryoshka Representation Learning (MRL)\nUsing Matryoshka loss, the first 256 dimensions encode coarse domain semantics while the full 1024 dimensions capture fine nuances. Two-stage funnel search scans 256-dim vectors in RAM for top-100 candidates and rescores with full 1024-dim vectors, reducing memory cost by 4x."}
+{"doc_id": "ML-OPS-005", "title": "Shadow Deployment, Canary Rollouts & Hallucination Guardrail Gates", "domain": "ml_operations", "version": "1.5", "owner": "MLOps Release Engineering", "text": "# Shadow Deployment, Canary Rollouts & Hallucination Guardrail Gates\n\n## Progressive Release Pipeline\nNew RAG configurations never jump straight to 100% traffic. Stage 1 runs 24-hour shadow traffic mirroring comparing candidate NDCG@5 and P99 latency against the champion pipeline. Stage 2 shifts 5% canary traffic stratified by tenant tier.\n\n## Automated Rollback Triggers\nArgo Rollouts automatically aborts the canary if P99 latency rises > 15%, unsupported claim rate exceeds 2.0%, or refusal accuracy on known unanswerable probes drops below 95%."}
+{"doc_id": "FIN-RISK-001", "title": "Basel III Liquidity Coverage Ratio (LCR) & Stress-Test Reporting Rules", "domain": "financial_risk", "version": "3.4", "owner": "Treasury Risk Analytics", "text": "# Basel III Liquidity Coverage Ratio (LCR) & Stress-Test Reporting Rules\n\n## Regulatory Threshold Formula\nUnder Basel III guidelines (`FIN-BASEL-LCR-105`), the Liquidity Coverage Ratio is defined as `LCR = High-Quality Liquid Assets (HQLA) / Total Net Cash Outflows over 30-day stress`. While the statutory regulatory floor is 100%, our internal treasury early-warning threshold is 112% and the management action trigger is 105%.\n\n## RAG Integration for Treasury Analysts\nAnalysts querying LCR haircut schedules (Level 1 assets: 0% haircut; Level 2A sovereign/agency bonds: 15% haircut; Level 2B corporate equities/bonds: 50% haircut) require exact numerical preservation. All numeric tables must remain intact inside single parent chunks."}
+{"doc_id": "FIN-RISK-002", "title": "SR 11-7 Model Risk Management for Generative AI & RAG Systems", "domain": "financial_risk", "version": "2.0", "owner": "Model Risk Governance Committee", "text": "# SR 11-7 Model Risk Management for Generative AI & RAG Systems\n\n## Federal Reserve SR 11-7 Validation Requirements\nAny LLM or RAG workflow informing credit underwriting, fraud triage, or regulatory disclosures is classified as a Tier-1 Model under Federal Reserve guidance SR 11-7. Validation requires:\n1. Conceptual soundness documentation (chunking, RRF fusion weights, prompt templates).\n2. Ongoing outcome analysis using golden ground-truth benchmarks and faithfulness scores.\n3. Deterministic fallback procedures when upstream LLM APIs exhibit latency spikes or drift.\n\n## Reproducibility Mandate\nEvery generated risk memo stores the exact `index_snapshot_id`, `model_checkpoint`, and chunk hashes so independent model validators can reproduce citations months later."}
+{"doc_id": "FIN-RISK-003", "title": "Real-Time Fraud Detection Feature Store & RAG Case Investigator", "domain": "financial_risk", "version": "2.6", "owner": "Fraud Science Engineering", "text": "# Real-Time Fraud Detection Feature Store & RAG Case Investigator\n\n## Combining Tabular Anomaly Scores with Policy RAG\nWhen the XGBoost transaction scorer flags a charge above risk score 0.88, fraud investigators receive an automated case brief synthesized via RAG over card-network chargeback rules (Visa Compelling Evidence 3.0 and Mastercard Reason Code 4837).\n\n## Latency & Accuracy Budget\nInvestigator briefs must assemble within 450 ms P95. Exact reason codes (`MC-4837`, `VISA-CE30`) are boosted via BM25 sparse retrieval while behavioral narrative summaries rely on dense embeddings."}
+{"doc_id": "FIN-RISK-004", "title": "Value at Risk (VaR) & Expected Shortfall Monte Carlo Governance", "domain": "financial_risk", "version": "1.9", "owner": "Quantitative Market Risk", "text": "# Value at Risk (VaR) & Expected Shortfall Monte Carlo Governance\n\n## FRTB Shift from VaR to Expected Shortfall\nUnder the Fundamental Review of the Trading Book (FRTB), desk capital models transition from 99% 10-day Value at Risk (VaR) to 97.5% Expected Shortfall (ES) to better capture tail risk beyond the quantile boundary.\n\n## Backtesting Exception Escalation\nKupiec POF backtesting tracks daily P&L exceptions over a 250-trading-day window: 0-4 exceptions stay in the Green Zone, 5-9 enter the Amber Zone (capital multiplier increases from 3.0 to 3.85), and 10+ trigger the Red Zone (`ERR_RISK_RED10`) requiring immediate model recalibration."}
+{"doc_id": "FIN-RISK-005", "title": "FinOps Token Cost Optimization & Per-Tenant Chargeback Model", "domain": "financial_risk", "version": "2.1", "owner": "Cloud & AI FinOps", "text": "# FinOps Token Cost Optimization & Per-Tenant Chargeback Model\n\n## Unit Economics at 10,000 Concurrent Requests\nAssuming 1,500 input tokens and 250 output tokens per cold RAG request, uncached traffic at 10,000 RPS would consume 17.5M tokens/sec. Achieving >70% combined L1+L2 cache hit rate plus prompt compression cuts inference spend by 74%.\n\n## Cost Attribution Formula\nTenant chargeback aggregates `(prompt_tokens * c_in + completion_tokens * c_out) * tier_margin` minus cache savings rebates. Queries routed to the local quantized 8B tier cost $0.00012 per request versus $0.0048 on frontier reasoning models—a 40x unit-cost reduction."}
+{"doc_id": "SLA-GOV-001", "title": "Enterprise Tier-0 SLA Contract, Error Budgets & Burn-Rate Alerts", "domain": "sla_governance", "version": "3.0", "owner": "Site Reliability Engineering", "text": "# Enterprise Tier-0 SLA Contract, Error Budgets & Burn-Rate Alerts\n\n## Availability & Latency Commitments\nUnder policy `SLA-TIER0-99.99`, Tier-0 Enterprise RAG endpoints guarantee 99.99% monthly uptime (maximum 4.32 minutes of downtime per 30-day month) and P95 end-to-end retrieval+first-token latency <= 400 ms (`P99 <= 850 ms`) up to 10,000 concurrent requests.\n\n## Multi-Window Error Budget Burn Alerts\nSRE paging triggers on two burn-rate windows simultaneously:\n- **Fast Burn (Page Immediate)**: 14.4x burn rate over 1 hour AND 5 minutes (consumes 2% of monthly budget in 1 hour).\n- **Slow Burn (Ticket)**: 3.0x burn rate over 6 hours AND 30 minutes.\nIf remaining monthly error budget drops below 10%, all non-emergency feature deployments freeze."}
+{"doc_id": "SLA-GOV-002", "title": "Circuit Breaker, Graceful Degradation & Chaos Engineering Runbook", "domain": "sla_governance", "version": "2.4", "owner": "Reliability & Chaos Team", "text": "# Circuit Breaker, Graceful Degradation & Chaos Engineering Runbook\n\n## Tri-State Circuit Breaker Mechanics\nTo prevent cascading timeouts when the upstream LLM provider degrades, the pipeline circuit breaker tracks rolling failures. After 10 consecutive upstream timeouts (CLOSED -> OPEN), the breaker stays OPEN for 15 seconds, automatically serving grounded extractive summaries directly from top-reranked chunks (`degraded_extractive_mode`) instead of returning HTTP 500 errors.\n\n## Half-Open Recovery & Chaos Drills\nAfter 15 seconds, the breaker transitions to HALF-OPEN and allows 3 probe requests. Monthly GameDay chaos drills inject 500 ms synthetic Qdrant jitter and kill 30% of gateway pods to verify 100% request completion within SLA error budgets."}
+{"doc_id": "SLA-GOV-003", "title": "Little's Law Capacity Planning for 10,000 Concurrent RAG Users", "domain": "sla_governance", "version": "1.8", "owner": "Capacity Engineering", "text": "# Little's Law Capacity Planning for 10,000 Concurrent RAG Users\n\n## Mathematical Sizing Model\nBy Little's Law, `L = lambda * W`, where `L` is average concurrency, `lambda` is arrival rate (RPS), and `W` is average service latency in seconds.\n- Suppose 10,000 concurrent users each trigger queries or wait in active request pipelines with average blended latency `W = 0.080s` (with 75% L1/L2 cache hits at 2 ms and 25% cold RAG at 310 ms): `lambda = 10,000 / 0.080 = 125,000 RPS` if all 10k are continuously in-flight, or for 10,000 simultaneous burst requests completing within 1.0 second, the cluster needs `>= 10,000 RPS` sustained capacity.\n\n## Pod & Cache Sizing\nAcross 32 async FastAPI/Uvicorn workers (4 workers per 8-vCPU pod), each worker holds 256 async concurrency slots (`8,192` active cold slots + zero-block cache paths), comfortably absorbing 10,000 simultaneous requests without thread exhaustion."}
+{"doc_id": "SLA-GOV-004", "title": "Incident Severity Matrix (SEV-1 to SEV-4) & Postmortem Policy", "domain": "sla_governance", "version": "2.2", "owner": "Incident Command", "text": "# Incident Severity Matrix (SEV-1 to SEV-4) & Postmortem Policy\n\n## Severity Classification\n- **SEV-1 (Critical)**: >5% 5xx rate, cross-tenant data leakage (`ERR_SEC_TENANT_4039`), or complete outage of Tier-0 RAG APIs. 15-minute page response, executive bridge open.\n- **SEV-2 (High)**: P99 latency > 2,000 ms for >10 minutes, cache cluster failover, or faithfulness score drop below 0.65.\n- **SEV-3 (Medium)**: Single-shard degraded replication or non-critical ingestion lag > 30 min.\n\n## Blameless Postmortem SLA\nAll SEV-1 and SEV-2 incidents require a blameless RCA document within 48 hours and golden regression test cases added to `data/eval/golden_qa.jsonl` within 5 business days."}
+{"doc_id": "SLA-GOV-005", "title": "Enterprise Knowledge Base Freshness, CDC Ingestion & Versioning SLA", "domain": "sla_governance", "version": "1.5", "owner": "Data Ingestion Platform", "text": "# Enterprise Knowledge Base Freshness, CDC Ingestion & Versioning SLA\n\n## Change Data Capture (CDC) Pipeline\nConfluence, SharePoint, Notion, and Git markdown repositories stream webhook deltas into Kafka. Documents undergo deduplication via MinHash LSH (Jaccard threshold 0.85), PII scrubbing, Parent-Child chunking, and incremental upsert.\n\n## Freshness & Atomic Version Cutover\nTier-0 compliance and incident runbooks carry a 5-minute P95 indexing freshness SLA (`SLA-FRESH-5M`). Bulk corpus re-embeddings write to a shadow collection (`corpus_v{N+1}`) and swap aliases atomically."}
+{"doc_id": "CLOUD-ARCH-006", "title": "Kubernetes HPA & KEDA Queue-Depth Autoscaling Policy", "domain": "cloud_architecture", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Cloud Architecture Team", "text": "# Kubernetes HPA & KEDA Queue-Depth Autoscaling Policy\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nKEDA scales FastAPI pods from 8 to 48 replicas when Redis request queue depth exceeds 400 or CPU crosses 65%. PodDisruptionBudgets preserve at least 75% capacity during node drains.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nERR_K8S_HPA_112 | Target Concurrency: 256 slots/pod | Scale-down stabilization: 300s\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `CLOUD-ARCH-006` for domain `cloud_architecture`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "CLOUD-ARCH-007", "title": "gRPC vs REST Internal Service Mesh Protocol Benchmarks", "domain": "cloud_architecture", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Cloud Architecture Team", "text": "# gRPC vs REST Internal Service Mesh Protocol Benchmarks\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nInternal calls between the API Gateway and Embedding/Reranker microservices use HTTP/2 gRPC with Protobuf payloads and Envoy round-robin load balancing, saving 38% serialization overhead versus JSON.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nERR_GRPC_DEADLINE_4 | Keepalive ping: 10s | Max message size: 16MB\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `CLOUD-ARCH-007` for domain `cloud_architecture`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "CLOUD-ARCH-008", "title": "Read-Replica Routing & Vector Snapshot Disaster Recovery", "domain": "cloud_architecture", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Cloud Architecture Team", "text": "# Read-Replica Routing & Vector Snapshot Disaster Recovery\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nCross-region disaster recovery replicates Qdrant snapshots every 15 minutes to dual-region object storage, achieving RPO <= 15 minutes and RTO <= 8 minutes during regional AZ isolation.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nDR-TIER0-RTO8 | Cross-region replication: us-east <-> us-west\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `CLOUD-ARCH-008` for domain `cloud_architecture`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "CLOUD-ARCH-009", "title": "Async Connection Pooling & Ephemeral Port Exhaustion Prevention", "domain": "cloud_architecture", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Cloud Architecture Team", "text": "# Async Connection Pooling & Ephemeral Port Exhaustion Prevention\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nHigh-concurrency Python workers reuse persistent httpx.AsyncClient pools with max_connections=512 and SO_REUSEADDR enabled, avoiding TIME_WAIT ephemeral port exhaustion at 10,000+ RPS.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nERR_PORT_9901 | Pool max_keepalive_connections: 256 | Keepalive expiry: 30s\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `CLOUD-ARCH-009` for domain `cloud_architecture`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "CLOUD-ARCH-010", "title": "BM25 Inverted Index Memory-Mapping & Stopword Tuning", "domain": "cloud_architecture", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Cloud Architecture Team", "text": "# BM25 Inverted Index Memory-Mapping & Stopword Tuning\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nSparse lexical indexes store postings lists in memory-mapped segments (`mmap`) with BM25 saturation `k1=1.5` and length normalization `b=0.75`. Technical identifiers and hyphens remain intact during tokenization.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nSPARSE-CFG-K15 | Custom tokenizer preserves codes like SOC2-CC6.7 and ERR_QDRANT_5032\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `CLOUD-ARCH-010` for domain `cloud_architecture`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "CLOUD-ARCH-011", "title": "Streaming Token Compression & Context Window Packing", "domain": "cloud_architecture", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Cloud Architecture Team", "text": "# Streaming Token Compression & Context Window Packing\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nBefore invoking the generator LLM, retrieved parent chunks are deduplicated by doc_id and ordered with highest-relevance snippets at the start and end ('primacy-recency packing') to counter lost-in-the-middle degradation.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nCTX-PACK-OPT | Max context budget: 3,200 tokens | Overlap merge threshold: 0.70\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `CLOUD-ARCH-011` for domain `cloud_architecture`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "CLOUD-ARCH-012", "title": "Edge CDN Static Asset Caching & SSE Keepalive Heartbeats", "domain": "cloud_architecture", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Cloud Architecture Team", "text": "# Edge CDN Static Asset Caching & SSE Keepalive Heartbeats\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nCloudflare Workers cache static workbench assets while disabling response buffering (`X-Accel-Buffering: no`) on `/api/v1/query/stream` SSE endpoints with 15-second comment heartbeats.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nSSE-CFG-15S | Proxy read timeout: 120s | Chunked transfer enabled\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `CLOUD-ARCH-012` for domain `cloud_architecture`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "CLOUD-ARCH-013", "title": "Cold-Start Elimination via Pre-Warmed Embedding Pools", "domain": "cloud_architecture", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Cloud Architecture Team", "text": "# Cold-Start Elimination via Pre-Warmed Embedding Pools\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nKubernetes startup probes wait until embedding SVD matrices, BM25 vocabulary tries, and HNSW indexes are memory-resident before joining Envoy service endpoints, eliminating cold-start latency spikes.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nPROBE-READY-200 | Pre-warm queries: 50 synthetic probes on boot\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `CLOUD-ARCH-013` for domain `cloud_architecture`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "SEC-COMP-006", "title": "SOC2 Type II Change Management & CI/CD Artifact Signing", "domain": "security_compliance", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Security Compliance Team", "text": "# SOC2 Type II Change Management & CI/CD Artifact Signing\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nEvery container image pushed to the production registry is signed with Sigstore Cosign and verified by Kyverno admission controllers before Kubernetes scheduling, enforcing SOC2-CC8.1.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nSOC2-CC8.1 | SBOM format: CycloneDX | Vulnerability gate: Zero Critical CVEs\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `SEC-COMP-006` for domain `security_compliance`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "SEC-COMP-007", "title": "Tenant Rate-Limit Isolation & Noisy-Neighbor Fair Queuing", "domain": "security_compliance", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Security Compliance Team", "text": "# Tenant Rate-Limit Isolation & Noisy-Neighbor Fair Queuing\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nDeficit Round Robin (DRR) weighted fair queuing prevents a single abusive tenant from starving shared worker pools, capping individual tenant burst at 20% of cluster capacity.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nERR_TENANT_QUOTA_429 | Per-tenant burst cap: 2,000 RPS | Shared pool protection\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `SEC-COMP-007` for domain `security_compliance`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "SEC-COMP-008", "title": "Synthetic Red-Teaming & Adversarial Jailbreak Benchmark Suite", "domain": "security_compliance", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Security Compliance Team", "text": "# Synthetic Red-Teaming & Adversarial Jailbreak Benchmark Suite\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nWeekly automated red-teaming executes 250 adversarial prompts testing system-prompt extraction, roleplay bypasses, and cross-tenant data probing; release gate requires >= 98% block rate.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nREDTEAM-GATE-98 | 250 probes | Automated OWASP LLM Top-10 coverage\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `SEC-COMP-008` for domain `security_compliance`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "SEC-COMP-009", "title": "KMS Envelope Key Rotation & Secret Injection via CSI Driver", "domain": "security_compliance", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Security Compliance Team", "text": "# KMS Envelope Key Rotation & Secret Injection via CSI Driver\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nApplication pods never store API keys in environment files on disk; secrets mount ephemerally into tmpfs via Secrets Store CSI Driver with automatic 30-day rotation.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nKMS-ROTATE-30D | Secret backend: Vault Enterprise | Zero plaintext secrets\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `SEC-COMP-009` for domain `security_compliance`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "SEC-COMP-010", "title": "Data Residency & EU Sovereign Region Routing Policy", "domain": "security_compliance", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Security Compliance Team", "text": "# Data Residency & EU Sovereign Region Routing Policy\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nEU customer workspaces enforce strict geo-fenced routing (`eu-central-1` only) for embeddings, L1/L2 caches, and inference endpoints to satisfy Schrems II and GDPR Chapter V.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nGEO-FENCE-EU | Allowed regions: eu-central-1, eu-west-1 | Cross-region replication disabled\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `SEC-COMP-010` for domain `security_compliance`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "SEC-COMP-011", "title": "Unanswerable Query Refusal & Groundedness Enforcement Standard", "domain": "security_compliance", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Security Compliance Team", "text": "# Unanswerable Query Refusal & Groundedness Enforcement Standard\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nWhen maximum retrieval confidence drops below the calibrated threshold (0.20) or context fails to entail the claim, the synthesizer must abstain cleanly rather than fabricate answers.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nREFUSAL-POL-020 | Groundedness target: >= 0.95 refusal precision on out-of-scope queries\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `SEC-COMP-011` for domain `security_compliance`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "SEC-COMP-012", "title": "Log Scrubbing & Observability Telemetry Anonymization", "domain": "security_compliance", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Security Compliance Team", "text": "# Log Scrubbing & Observability Telemetry Anonymization\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nOpenTelemetry traces and Prometheus labels must never emit raw user queries or PII; spans log hashed query fingerprints, latency histograms, and numerical retrieval scores only.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nOTEL-SCRUB-V2 | Allowed span attributes: query_hash, cache_tier, latency_ms\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `SEC-COMP-012` for domain `security_compliance`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "SEC-COMP-013", "title": "Vendor LLM Zero-Data-Retention (ZDR) Contractual Standard", "domain": "security_compliance", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Security Compliance Team", "text": "# Vendor LLM Zero-Data-Retention (ZDR) Contractual Standard\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nExternal foundation model APIs may only process enterprise prompts under signed Zero-Data-Retention addenda ensuring prompts and completions are never stored or used for model training.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nVENDOR-ZDR-01 | Mandatory header: X-Data-Retention: none | Quarterly vendor audit\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `SEC-COMP-013` for domain `security_compliance`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "ML-OPS-006", "title": "Golden Dataset Curation & Stratified Stratified Sampling Protocol", "domain": "ml_operations", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Ml Operations Team", "text": "# Golden Dataset Curation & Stratified Stratified Sampling Protocol\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nEnterprise evaluation sets maintain balanced coverage across exact lexical lookups, paraphrased conceptual questions, multi-hop synthesis, and unanswerable adversarial traps.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nEVAL-STRATA-4 | Minimum 40 curated QA pairs | Inter-annotator Cohen kappa >= 0.82\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `ML-OPS-006` for domain `ml_operations`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "ML-OPS-007", "title": "Cross-Encoder vs ColBERT Late-Interaction Reranker Tradeoffs", "domain": "ml_operations", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Ml Operations Team", "text": "# Cross-Encoder vs ColBERT Late-Interaction Reranker Tradeoffs\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nFull cross-encoders deliver maximum accuracy (+18% MRR) at 25-40 ms for top-20 passages, whereas ColBERT late-interaction precomputes token embeddings for 6 ms reranking under strict latency SLAs.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nRERANK-BUDGET-20 | Candidate pool N=20 | Final context K=5\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `ML-OPS-007` for domain `ml_operations`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "ML-OPS-008", "title": "Query Rewriting, HyDE & Multi-Query Expansion Guidelines", "domain": "ml_operations", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Ml Operations Team", "text": "# Query Rewriting, HyDE & Multi-Query Expansion Guidelines\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nHypothetical Document Embeddings (HyDE) improves recall on vague conceptual questions by +7% but adds 180 ms LLM overhead; thus HyDE activates only when initial BM25+Dense score < 0.35.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nHYDE-COND-035 | Conditional activation saves 82% extra LLM rewrite calls\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `ML-OPS-008` for domain `ml_operations`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "ML-OPS-009", "title": "Semantic Cache Threshold Calibration (Precision-Recall ROC Curve)", "domain": "ml_operations", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Ml Operations Team", "text": "# Semantic Cache Threshold Calibration (Precision-Recall ROC Curve)\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nSweeping L2 semantic similarity threshold tau from 0.80 to 0.96 shows tau=0.90 achieves 31% semantic cache hit rate while keeping false-positive cache collisions under 0.8%.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nL2-TAU-090 | Optimal operating point: cosine >= 0.90 | False-hit rate < 0.8%\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `ML-OPS-009` for domain `ml_operations`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "ML-OPS-010", "title": "Deduplication with MinHash LSH for Enterprise Document Ingestion", "domain": "ml_operations", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Ml Operations Team", "text": "# Deduplication with MinHash LSH for Enterprise Document Ingestion\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nNear-duplicate Wiki pages and email threads inflate vector indexes and crowd out diverse top-5 sources. MinHash LSH (128 permutations, Jaccard >= 0.85) collapses redundant copies before indexing.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nDEDUP-LSH-85 | Storage reduction: 29% | Diversity gain in top-5: +16%\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `ML-OPS-010` for domain `ml_operations`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "ML-OPS-011", "title": "Citation Grounding Verification via NLI Entailment Scoring", "domain": "ml_operations", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Ml Operations Team", "text": "# Citation Grounding Verification via NLI Entailment Scoring\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nEach generated sentence containing a `[doc_id]` citation is scored by an NLI cross-checker verifying Entailment >= 0.70 against the cited parent chunk before streaming completion.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nNLI-ENTAIL-070 | Unsupported claims trigger inline caveat or regeneration\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `ML-OPS-011` for domain `ml_operations`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "ML-OPS-012", "title": "Offline Feature & Embedding Lineage Tracking in MLflow", "domain": "ml_operations", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Ml Operations Team", "text": "# Offline Feature & Embedding Lineage Tracking in MLflow\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nEvery corpus build records embedding model SHA, SVD explained variance, chunker config, and dataset checksum in MLflow artifacts to enable exact rollback of retrieval regressions.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nMLFLOW-LINEAGE | Artifact tags: chunker, rrf_k, embedding_dim, corpus_sha256\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `ML-OPS-012` for domain `ml_operations`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "ML-OPS-013", "title": "Active Learning Loop from Thumbs-Down & Low-Confidence Feedback", "domain": "ml_operations", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Ml Operations Team", "text": "# Active Learning Loop from Thumbs-Down & Low-Confidence Feedback\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nUser thumbs-down events and queries with faithfulness < 0.60 enter Label Studio queues weekly, producing curated hard-negative triples and expanding the golden benchmark.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nAL-LOOP-WEEKLY | SLA: 50 new labeled edge cases per sprint\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `ML-OPS-013` for domain `ml_operations`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "FIN-RISK-006", "title": "Credit Underwriting Policy RAG & Adverse Action Notice Grounding", "domain": "financial_risk", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Financial Risk Team", "text": "# Credit Underwriting Policy RAG & Adverse Action Notice Grounding\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nUnder ECOA Regulation B, automated credit denial rationales generated with RAG assistance must cite exact underwriting rule identifiers and verified income/DTI threshold tables.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nECOA-REGB-44 | Max DTI standard cap: 43% | Mandatory rule citation ID\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `FIN-RISK-006` for domain `financial_risk`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "FIN-RISK-007", "title": "Anti-Money Laundering (AML) SAR Narrative Synthesis Controls", "domain": "financial_risk", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Financial Risk Team", "text": "# Anti-Money Laundering (AML) SAR Narrative Synthesis Controls\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nSuspicious Activity Report (SAR) drafts incorporate transaction structuring patterns ($9,000-$9,999 cash deposits) and FinCEN advisory codes while blocking speculative legal conclusions.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nAML-SAR-31CFR | Structuring threshold review: $10,000 cumulative 24h\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `FIN-RISK-007` for domain `financial_risk`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "FIN-RISK-008", "title": "Counterparty Credit Exposure & CVA Sensitivity Calculation Standard", "domain": "financial_risk", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Financial Risk Team", "text": "# Counterparty Credit Exposure & CVA Sensitivity Calculation Standard\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nCredit Valuation Adjustment (CVA) desks compute Potential Future Exposure (PFE) at the 95th percentile across netting sets with ISDA Credit Support Annex (CSA) collateral thresholds.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nCVA-PFE-95 | Margin Period of Risk (MPOR): 10 business days\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `FIN-RISK-008` for domain `financial_risk`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "FIN-RISK-009", "title": "Algorithmic Trading Pre-Trade Kill-Switch & Fat-Finger Limits", "domain": "financial_risk", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Financial Risk Team", "text": "# Algorithmic Trading Pre-Trade Kill-Switch & Fat-Finger Limits\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nSEC Rule 15c3-5 mandates hard pre-trade notional order caps ($25M single order) and price collar checks (+/- 3% from NBBO midpoint) enforced in hardware before exchange routing.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nSEC-15C3-5 | Kill-switch trigger latency: < 50 microseconds\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `FIN-RISK-009` for domain `financial_risk`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "FIN-RISK-010", "title": "IFRS 9 Expected Credit Loss (ECL) Stage Migration Criteria", "domain": "financial_risk", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Financial Risk Team", "text": "# IFRS 9 Expected Credit Loss (ECL) Stage Migration Criteria\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nFinancial assets migrate from Stage 1 (12-month ECL) to Stage 2 (lifetime ECL) upon Significant Increase in Credit Risk (SICR), triggered by >30 days past due or 2-notch PD downgrade.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nIFRS9-SICR-30D | Stage 3 default trigger: >= 90 days past due\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `FIN-RISK-010` for domain `financial_risk`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
+{"doc_id": "FIN-RISK-011", "title": "Sanctions Screening Fuzzy Matching & OFAC List Sync SLA", "domain": "financial_risk", "version": "1.0", "owner": "Financial Risk Team", "text": "# Sanctions Screening Fuzzy Matching & OFAC List Sync SLA\n\n## Policy & Engineering Specification\nOFAC SDN list updates sync within 15 minutes across screening engines combining Jaro-Winkler phonetic scoring (threshold 0.88) with BM25 alias token matching.\n\n## Operational Thresholds & Identifiers\nOFAC-SYNC-15M | Jaro-Winkler threshold: 0.88 | Zero false-negative tolerance\n\n## Cross-Functional Governance\nThis document is governed under enterprise standard `FIN-RISK-011` for domain `financial_risk`. Automated CI checks verify adherence during pre-production benchmarking and canary rollouts."}
